Regarding the drift rate (TRUE-FALSE), or the signal-to-noise ratio provided by the stimulus, visual inspections of the predictions show that, as car recognition ability increases, only the drift rate for Novel faces increases, whereas the drift rate for Learned face does not follow this pattern. In summary, as car recognition ability increases, the ability to discriminate Novel faces increases but not the ability to discriminate Learned faces (@fig-prediction-drift-constrast-car).




